  "id": "kriging",
  "term": "kriging",
  "definition": "Kriging is a method for turning measurements taken at specific locations into a continuous map of predicted values across an area. It uses assumptions about how nearby locations are spatially related, and ordinary kriging in particular depends on modeling that spatial pattern from sufficiently dense samples.",
